WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.969
 

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:14.547
That's just how life is
on Earth 2.0

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:15.915
Double the density,

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:40.273
This is 'What If,'

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:44.077
and here's what would happen
if Earth's gravity were to double.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:47.647
See how the Earth
moves around the Sun?

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:51.251
Its current elliptical path
gives us winter and summer,

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:54.054
without bringing us
too close to our star.

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:58.024
Since the Sun is 330,000 times
heavier than Earth,

00:00:58.024 --> 00:01:01.761
its gravitational influence
pulls the Earth towards it.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:05.031
Luckily, our planet moves
sideways from the Sun's pull,

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:05.932
and fast enough,

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:10.236
so that it doesn't get sucked
into that giant ball of hot plasma.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:15.675
But up the gravity on Earth by just
a little bit, and you ruin everything.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:19.212
If Earth's gravity was just 5% stronger,

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:23.183
the increase would warp our planet's
near-perfect circlular orbit

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:25.518
into a tighter elliptical path.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:28.721
Summers and winters would
become a lot harsher,

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:31.858
the intense climate change
would spark widespread famine

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:34.861
and would likely collapse
the world economy.

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:37.764
And yet, there might
be some survivors.

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:40.700
That's just from a 5% difference.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:48.007
Let's put climate concerns
aside for a moment.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:51.611
Realistically, we just wouldn't
survive a drastic change.

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:55.115
The Earth's core would probably
just collapse in on itself,

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:57.150
causing everyone to
fall to their deaths,

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:01.554
or releasing enough heat
to cook us all alive!

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:06.426
But let's imagine that gravity doubles
at a rate that allows us to keep our lives,

00:02:06.426 --> 00:02:08.828
so we can try this new world out.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:12.866
Well, to be honest, there
isn't much to look forward to.

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.701
You're now twice as heavy.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.170
And while that might sound
like a gift to some of you,

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:20.039
it won't be unless
you're in great shape...

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:23.877
Your heart and lungs will be
strained under the increased pressure.

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:27.547
Breathing gets harder, and
your blood pressure skyrockets.

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:32.819
Imagine, you're basically giving
yourself a piggyback ride 24/7.

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:39.959
Sleeping gives you bed sores, stairs get scary,
and trips and falls might even become fatal!

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:45.398
Speaking of falls, our infrastructure,
our technology, and nature itself,

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:48.067
aren't equipped to handle
this type of force.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.403
Buckling under twice the
weight they were built for,

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:53.273
buildings and bridges would collapse;

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:54.774
planes would also fall from the sky;

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:57.310
and satellites would
tumble back to Earth;

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:01.314
since they’d no longer be traveling
at the right orbital velocity.

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:03.683
Trees would collapse
under their own weight,

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:07.921
or they would die from not being able
to pump water as high as they used to.

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:11.357
New ones growing in their place
would be much shorter and thicker

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:14.627
in order to accomodate the
new constraints of double gravity.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:18.665
And like that, perhaps humans
would evolve the same way:

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:23.069
decreased height, thicker veins,
increased bone density.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:25.271
Barring the severe climate change
that would occur,

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.073
such as atmospheric compression

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:29.275
and increased radioactivity,

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:33.112
we might actually be able to
build a nice little life for ourselves.

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:37.250
That is, one where everything is
smaller and a closer to the ground,

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:39.152
but what's wrong with that anyway?

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:42.121
Double gravity or not, life is short!

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.824
So try something new,
let your mind wander,

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:55.235
and circle back for more 'What If.'

